\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Lesion volume and uptake change of ground-truth lesions, grouped by how much of each lesion the predicted lesion mask seen by IO covers: missed (214 lesions, 6\,\% of volume), partly covered (155 lesions, 6\,\% of volume), covered (1066 lesions, 88\,\% of volume). Test set; network trained without PET losses, IO with the PET weights scaled by the given factor. Left: change within each group (per scan, the change of the summed volume or uptake of the group's lesions; mean over the patients with lesions in the group). Right: contribution of each group to the evaluation metric (the change per scan if only the group's lesions changed; mean over patients); black: the evaluation metric, below the stacked total because changes of different lesions in a scan partly cancel.}}{24}{figure.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:detection}{{7}{24}{Lesion volume and uptake change of ground-truth lesions, grouped by how much of each lesion the predicted lesion mask seen by IO covers: missed (214 lesions, 6\,\% of volume), partly covered (155 lesions, 6\,\% of volume), covered (1066 lesions, 88\,\% of volume). Test set; network trained without PET losses, IO with the PET weights scaled by the given factor. Left: change within each group (per scan, the change of the summed volume or uptake of the group's lesions; mean over the patients with lesions in the group). Right: contribution of each group to the evaluation metric (the change per scan if only the group's lesions changed; mean over patients); black: the evaluation metric, below the stacked total because changes of different lesions in a scan partly cancel}{figure.7}{}}
